y flavor but some  people think it can be a little bit  tough  whereas chuck is a little bit more fatty  tender subdued so the combination of  both is gonna give me a very strongly  flavored beefy burger as well as one  that's still juicy and tender when it  comes to the meat and fat ratio for the  meat I like 80% protein and 20% fat so  once you have your ground beef mixed  together I want to be 1/2 a pound  because I'm not here for no skimpy  burger it's really important to get it a  little bit bigger than the size of your  bun that way when it cooks it kind of  shrinks down to be the exact same  diameter and I press down the center to  get a little bit of a bevel that way  when the burger cooks it ends up being a  flat burger once you have all your  patties ready make sure your cast iron  is really hot I had a little bit of  butter into the pan and then I place  down the burger for my burgers I like to  just put it in the pan and cook it until  it has a nice char on one side I flip it  over once more until the other side is  good to go and then it comes right off  after you take the burgers out of the  pan it's time to toast your beautiful  pretzel buns the reason why I like  pretzel buns is because you have a  crispy top and if you toast the bun in  the same pan you have a crispy bottom  and allows all that flavor from the beef  fat to soak into your bun okay and now  it's time to assemble this honker take  the bottom bun smear on some ketchup put  on your beautiful caramelized onions  place the charred juicy burger your  butter lettuce thinly sliced tomato  pickled onion don't worry about those  electrodes or show you how to make those  in a bit then put the aioli and that is  time to eat  the reason I love my burger is because  it's a perfect balance of flavors  textures and temperatures I'm a  Midwestern boy so I love a burger that's  gonna make me full I want to be hefty  and I want to be able to taste each and  every bite so this is my perfect  decadent burger but if you want  something extremely flavorful you have  to try kimonos because her dozen be like  really flavorful god that's on camera if  you want a burger that you can't buy in  any restaurant and you have to try  making my burger my philosophy for  making a really really good hamburger is  uniformity everything should be the same  throughout that way every single bite is  just as delicious from beginning to end  tomato onion are notorious for slipping  and sliding out of burgers so to resolve  that I make a tomato jam tomato jam is  so great because it replaces three  essential items to your burger it serves  as a ketchup it's a tomato and it's the  onion all in one delicious spread you  chuck it all in a pot bring it to a boil  then you turn it down and let it bubble  away for about a half-hour second sauce  is really simple equal parts Dijon  mustard and a good-quality mayonnaise  mix well together let it hang out until  it's ready to assemble the bun is what  holds this whole perfect beautiful  burger together I like using that  classic you know burger bun those little  white sesame seeds on top I think  probably could use reminding my  childhood and they're just really cute  all it needs is a nice healthy spread of  butter and a little bit of time on that  cast-iron pan just enough to get golden  brown only on the inside they don't  toast the outside then I pop them aside  until  I appreciate all kinds of meat for my  burger but beef still king for me 80%  20% fat the important part for me is the  size of the patty in order to have a  nice uniform burger the patty needs to  be equal size to the bun however once  the patty goes on to the pan it's gonna  shrink a little bit  so I sheet made patty to be one inch  wider in diameter then my buns so once  it shrinks down it should be nice and  even on the sides so once my patties are  ready to go I cook them in a very hot  cast-iron skillet just long enough so  it'll golden crust forms on one side  flip it once but never press otherwise I  press out all the juice and a be a  driver burger and nobody likes to drive  after the cheese is on add a little bit  of water to the pan and pop on the lid  what this does it creates is nice you  know little steamy spa for the burger  where cheese can melt quickly without me  worrying about that burger drying out my  preferred cheese is a classic white  English cheddar it's strong enough yet a  little bit of nuttiness and oh man this  is so good  cooking the burger patty has to be the  very last stop this ensures that when  that burger hits the table it is still  hot and juicy and so they're so good  otherwise it'd be a nice little cute  local burger I could be old I'm talking  about like I ain't got no teeth old I  would need somebody to make me a pair of  dentures just so I can eat a burger as  my last meal on earth and that that's  how much I love burgers so ok ha the  tastiest burger I've ever made is my  smash burger I'm pretty classic in terms  of my tastes and that is what this  burger is it's not fussy it's really  classic  and I don't know anyone who would like  I'm gonna start with the pickled red  onions I love these onions because  so easy to make they add this great  crunch and it's not too acidic it has  some sweetness so you can actually do  this before you make your burger so that  the time they're all fried up you're  ready to go at the apple cider vinegar  the water sugar and salt into a small  pan and bring it to a boil over high  heat and then take it off the heat add  the onions and just let it sit at room  temperature for 30 minutes to an hour  and you can use it that's it simple this  so moving on to the burger I'm gonna use  80/20 so there's two types of burgers a  diner style burger and a pub style  burger you can really see the difference  with a diner style burger it's about  four ounces and it's really it's much  smaller and flatter whereas a pub style  burger is much thicker so before forming  it into a patty shape you're actually  gonna form it into a bowl and season it  generously with salt and pepper I'm  gonna use a cast-iron pan because it's  gonna give a great crust add the ball to  the cast-iron and then immediately take  a spatula or two and press it down  flattening the burger I like a thin  burger because you really get the flavor  of that crispy exterior I also think it  lets your toppings shine a bit more so  after you cook it for 1 to 2 minutes  flip it over that's what I'm gonna add  the cheese so I want that cheese to  really melt and cover that burger you  get that any gooey feeling from here  just cook it another minute or two and  then immediately take it off the heat  the bun I like to use is a brioche bun  some people think it's too sweet but I  actually think the sweetness is really  nice with the fat and the cheese and the  pickles all these elements coming  together just toast it until it's golden  brown just like this oh my god it's  perfect in terms of condiments are still  gonna keep it classic I'm just gonna mix  some ketchup and mayo to build my burger  I'm going to put the ketchup and mayo  mixture on both buns at the lettuce add  the burger patty tomato pickled onions  there you go that's my burger it's very  simple this is a really quick simple  burger but that's what I like about it  you know fancy burgers are too  but when I crave a burger this is what I  picture so now that you've seen all of  our favorite burger recipes you have to  make one yourself at home or share what  your favorite recipe is in the comments  or really just much like mine you  kidding me make mine classic burger make  mine mine's incredible you're not even  trying to fight yeah because Irene I  already want  [Applause]  [Music]

